Z||000000||fropuff||10-07-2000||12:14 AM||||Hey, I started a thread about glassing in rockcrawl's scoop.  Well, rockcrawl did a "smudging" to make it look like it was glassed in.  I think it would look really nice!  I especially like the one on the right side.  I want the mirror image on the left.  If I do get one, which would be in a while when they are made again, I would want to do this.  I was wondering if there is a way that I can "glass" in, or fill in, the "inward curves" on the left side panel.  I want it to look like the right, but on the left.  Is there a way I can do this?  Thanks.  You can see what I'm talking about on:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003885.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003885.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||contra||10-07-2000||09:29 AM||||you should be able to just glass it in fine<BR>take off the grill on your intake scoop and take a look<BR>if you've ever worked with fiberglass before, it should be fairly easy.<P>you will need to repaint the whole panel, in case you didn't know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
